abstract: >-
  EchoSpiro is a sovereign, zero-external-hardware pulmonary triage workstation that transforms
  commodity consumer electronics into an active continuous-wave (18.50 kHz) ultrasonic Doppler radar.
  Operating entirely within client volatile memory via the W3C Web Audio API, EchoSpiro quantifies
  chest-wall kinematic excursion, respiratory rate, I:E ratio, and acoustic wheeze patterns with gold-standard
  pneumotachography concordance (r = 0.968, MAE ±0.78 BPM) without patient contact or physical infection vectors.
